  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Escalation of violence in Gaza has left a significant number of civilians killed &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; wounded, with over 330K displaced. The violence has damaged shelters &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; infrastructure. The situation is becoming increasingly dire. Even before Oct-23, over 80% of Gazans needed humanitarian aid. Because of politically driven pressure, some donors have stopped/cut aid, creating severe service gaps. With the complete seize imposed, ppl. are struggling to secure cash to support their basic needs to buy food, water &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; medicine. Thousands have lost their homes and are now forced into temporary shelters, facing multiple protection risks. Shutdown of Gaza&apos;s power plant due to lack of fuel &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; hundreds of Israeli military airstrikes have destroyed essential WASH infrastructures &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;public services. This raises fears that Gaza will run out of electricity &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; water imminently.
The WASH sector faces multiple challenges, including access and distribution of materials and items necessary for WASH facilities. Israel&apos;s decision to cut water supply and electricity has impacted 5 WASH infrastructures &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; facilities, which served over 600K people. Gaza&apos;s current electricity generation is less than 60 MW, falling significantly short of the necessary power to sustain WASH services across the entire Gaza.
Against this backdrop Oxfam and local partners PEF, AISHA &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; CMWU propose to assist 18K people in Gaza city &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; North Gaza, with WASH &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; protection assistance incl. repair of damaged WASH networks aligning with Cluster response prioritization and Oxfam&apos;s expertise, distribute Hygiene Kit E-vouchers, including menstrual hygiene items &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; mitigating protection related risks, by supporting women and children whose needs are deprioritized in crises. Needs have been discussed with JR partners in Gaza to identify complementary activities and avoid duplication. Oxfam is well-positioned to respond with a well-established WASH program, focusing on strategic interventions in water systems &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; infrastructure for long-term impact</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
